{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1790191936,"nonce":"r5OzdkqsXNsNjPR0sy8tDz5MD5g=","target":"e61c43cd0f863c119e2519dad629829b01500c18303d612ac5ec620120065f68","message":"The generated `gpu` namespace covers basic compute, buffer readback, rendering\nand presentation, but does not yet cover the full wgpu feature set.\n\nThe vendored WebGPU IDL is generative input and a baseline, not the plugin's\ncontract or ceiling. Use it to generate portable interfaces, descriptors,\nenums and constants, then expose wgpu-only and native backend capabilities\nbehind adapter feature checks as well.\n\nMissing portable groups:\n\n- adapter features and complete limits, plus required feature/limit device negotiation;\n- explicit bind-group and pipeline layouts, dynamic offsets and binding ranges;\n- full texture/view/sampler descriptors, storage textures, dimensions, mips, layers and multisampling;\n- complete format catalogs (105 texture and 42 vertex formats in the vendored IDL; six and four exported now);\n- programmable constants, complete render-pass load/store state and full draw ranges;\n- query sets, timestamps, occlusion, render bundles and external textures/images;\n- error scopes, device-lost events and structured compilation messages;\n- configurable surface usage, present/alpha modes, view formats, color space and latency.\n\nMissing wgpu extensions outside the IDL include native format features,\npipeline statistics, encoder/pass timestamps, unrestricted mapped buffers,\nbinding arrays and non-uniform indexing, multi-draw, texture atomics, 64-bit\nshaders, subgroups, mesh shaders and ray tracing. Each remains conditional on\nadapter/backend support.\n\nThe target layer is prepared separately: the crate compile-checks for Metal,\nDX12, Vulkan, Android Vulkan/GLES, browser WebGPU and Emscripten GLES. Buffer\nsizes/ranges/offsets and reported limits remain 64-bit through the Caribou ABI.\nAdd conformance fixtures as groups land rather than treating a successful\ntarget compile as complete API coverage.","files":null}]}